- Added EJBCA as a certificate authority type (Fleet Premium). Add it in **Settings > Integrations > Certificate authorities**, with the API, or with GitOps (`org_settings.certificate_authorities.ejbca`), and use the `$FLEET_VAR_EJBCA_DATA_<name>` and `$FLEET_VAR_EJBCA_PASSWORD_<name>` variables in the PKCS#12 payload of a macOS, iOS, or iPadOS configuration profile to deliver a certificate to each host. The list of certificate authorities shows when the client certificate that Fleet uses to authenticate to EJBCA expires.
- Editing an EJBCA certificate authority's common name, username, UPN, CA name, or certificate or end entity profile name, in the UI, API, or GitOps, now reissues certificates to every host that has a certificate from that certificate authority.
- A configuration profile that can't get a certificate from an EJBCA or DigiCert certificate authority, because the certificate authority is temporarily unavailable, is now retried up to 3 times before it is marked as failed.
